;; Console mock world — the single source of truth for the mock fleet.
;; `bb console` copies this seed to tmp/console/world.edn and reads/writes THAT
;; file on every tick: edit the live copy to drive peers, delete it to reseed.
;;
;; :peers   — the wire shape both panels ride. Circle reads the shared core
;;            ({:id :name :online :desktop :apps :audio}); Setup adds :system
;;            (:clock-off-min = drift from true time — the wire carries the
;;            computed :now instead), :keyboard and :warns. A peer without
;;            [:apps :catalog] gets the top-level :catalog.
;; :removed — the panel's forgotten machines (remove is not a ban: a rescan
;;            revives them online — deliberate mock theater).
;; :knobs   — mock-only reply behavior per peer id, gone when the real
;;            transport lands: {:reply :ok|:fail|:noreply, :delay-ms 500,
;;            :checks {:gateway :fail}} (:checks overrides derived results)
